WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.240
Secure application development matters because applications often process, display,

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.100
transmit, or influence access to sensitive business and defense information.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.400
Weak application controls can expose Controlled Unclassified Information,

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:19.100
expand attack surface, or undermine evidence needed for assessment readiness.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.680
OWASP provides community-driven application security guidance.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.940
The OWASP Top 10 gives developers, DevSecOps teams, security engineers,

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.520
and compliance teams a shared vocabulary for common and high-impact web application risks.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:39.580
CMMC 2.0 is a cybersecurity model for defense contractors and organizations in the defense

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.520
industrial base. Level 1 focuses on foundational safeguarding practices,

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:49.540
while Level 2 aligns with NIST SP 800-171 requirements for protecting CUI.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:54.000
Application security supports CMMC by reducing software attack surface,

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:58.220
strengthening authentication and access control, improving monitoring,

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.160
and helping teams demonstrate that secure development and operational controls are

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.140
understood and repeatable.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:10.480
Each module explains an OWASP risk, practical attack scenarios, mitigations,

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:13.180
and selected CMMC practice mappings.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:18.040
These mappings are awareness aids and must be validated against the organization's actual

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.140
CMMC scope. Use OWASP categories to organize application risk discussions.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:28.320
Use CMMC practice domains to connect engineering work to CUI protection responsibilities.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:32.540
Validate mappings with the organization's security and compliance teams.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:40.440
Selected CMMC mappings for this topic include RA.L2-3.11.1 - Risk assessments;

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:51.060
CA.L2-3.12.1 - Security assessments; SI.L2-3.14.2 - Flaw remediation.
